  "answer": "Changes made (only the five writable files):\n\n- **`normalize.mjs`** — `normalizeIssue` no longer mutates input. It validates via `assertIssue`, then builds a fresh object in order `id, title, tags, assignee`: ID/title trimmed (case preserved), tags trimmed + `toLowerCase()` + empty-dropped + first-occurrence de-duplicated into a new array, assignee trimmed/lowercased with empty → `null` (input `null` stays `null`).\n- **`consumers/list.mjs`** — validates array (`TypeError('issues must be an array')`), maps to normalized issues in input order (no sorting, no in-place `sort` of the caller's array), duplicates preserved.\n- **`consumers/search.mjs`** — validates query string, uses `listIssues`, trims/lowercases query, empty query returns the whole normalized list, otherwise substring match on normalized title or any normalized tag (not IDs/assignees), original order, fresh array per call.\n- **`consumers/activity.mjs`** — uses `listIssues`; renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags (empty tags → empty final field).\n- **`serialize.mjs`** — serializes `listIssues(issues)` so order and property order match the list view and extra fields are dropped.\n\nUnchanged: `legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, `validators.mjs`, fixtures, date/paging/console helpers. No tests were executed (no shell available); correctness was checked by reading the code against the stated contract and the example in `public.test.mjs`.",
